.TH GLASSOSDCTL 1 "2026-08-29" "glassosd" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glassosdctl \- control and configure a running glassosd
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glassosdctl
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Drives the daemon over D\-Bus and writes
.BR glassosdrc (5).
Nearly every setting applies live; the exceptions are noted.
.PP
Most commands print their current value when given no argument, so the same
command reads and writes.
.SH STATE
.TP
.B status
Daemon state and every current setting.
.TP
.B version
Daemon version.
.TP
.BI "get " key
Read a Notifications setting.
.TP
.BI "set " "key value"
Write a Notifications setting.
.TP
.B restart
Restart the daemon. Needed only after changing
.BR Modules .
.TP
.B log
Follow the journal.
.SH NOTIFICATIONS
.TP
.BR dnd " [on|off|toggle]"
Do Not Disturb.
.TP
.BR history " [show|hide]"
Open or close the notification centre.
.TP
.B dismiss
Close every popup on screen, including ones with
.B expire_timeout 0
or critical urgency, which the specification requires to stay until acted on.
.TP
.BI "search " text
Open the centre with history filtered to
.IR text .
.TP
.BR snooze " [" minutes ]
How long the snooze button defers a notification. Default 10.
.TP
.B snoozed
What is snoozed, and when each is due.
.TP
.BR badge " [on|off]"
Mark the tray icon when notifications arrived while the centre was closed. The
count is in the tooltip, because no icon theme ships numerals.
.TP
.B test
Fire the demo sequence.
.TP
.BR export " [" file "] [" \-\-with\-history ]
Save settings, rules, focus modes, buttons and your themes to a tarball.
History and snoozed wake times are left out unless
.B \-\-with\-history
is given: they are a record of what happened on one machine rather than
configuration, and restoring one machine's backlog onto another is not what
"my config" means.
.TP
.BI "import " file
Restore an export. What is already there is backed up first, since restoring a
configuration should never be the thing that loses one. Modules are read at
startup, so follow with
.BR restart .
.SH RULES AND FOCUS MODES
.TP
.B rules
List notification rules.
.TP
.BI "rule\-set " "name key=value ..."
Create or update a rule. See
.BR glassosdrc (5)
for the matchers and actions.
.TP
.BI "rule\-del " name
Delete a rule.
.TP
.BR focus " [" name |off]
Switch focus mode.
.TP
.BI "focus\-set " name
.RB [ allow= A,B ]
.RB [ block= C,D ]
Define or amend a mode.
.TP
.BI "focus\-del " name
Delete a mode.
.TP
.BR quiet\-while\-busy " [on|off]"
Stay quiet while an application is holding the screen awake. Off by default,
and not literal fullscreen: a Wayland client cannot see that.
.SH OSD
.TP
.BR "osd volume" " [raise|lower|mute|" 0\-100 ]
.TQ
.BR "osd mic" " [mute|" 0\-100 ]
.TQ
.BR "osd brightness" " [raise|lower|" 0\-100 ]
.TQ
.BI "osd text " "icon text"
Bind these to your compositor's media keys when you are not on Plasma. On
Plasma the OSD is driven automatically and they are not needed.
.SH APPEARANCE
.TP
.BR theme " [dark|light]"
Light or dark palette.
.TP
.BR theme\-file " [" name ]
Load a JSON theme.
.TP
.B themes
List available themes and where they live.
.TP
.B edit\-theme
Copy the current theme to
.I ~/.config/glassosd/
and open it.
.TP
.BR accent " [" #rrggbb ]
Accent colour. Darkened automatically if it would fail contrast.
.TP
.BR scale " [0.6\-2.0]"
Size multiplier for all text and spacing.
.TP
.BR font " [6\-32]"
Text point size, independent of scale. Use this for bigger text in the same
layout. 0 or
.B auto
derives it from scale.
.TP
.BR width " [240\-900]"
Popup width in logical pixels.
.TP
.BR solidity " [0.0\-1.0]"
Push glass toward opaque. 0 keeps the tuned glass; raise it on compositors that
do not blur.
.TP
.BR level " [segmented|bar]"
Volume and brightness indicator style.
.TP
.BR lines " [1\-20]"
.TQ
.BR centre\-lines " [1\-20]"
Body lines a popup, and an entry in the centre, show before eliding. Defaults 4
and 3.
.SH PLACEMENT
.TP
.BR position " [" where ]
Which corner or edge popups appear at:
.BR top\-left ,
.BR top\-centre ,
.B top\-right
(default),
.BR bottom\-left ,
.BR bottom\-centre ,
.BR bottom\-right .
.TP
.BR offset " [" X "] [" Y ]
Extra clearance from the anchored screen edges, in logical pixels. 0 is not
flush, since the shadow already insets the cards. One number sets both.
.TP
.BR centre\-position " [left|right]"
Which side the notification centre slides in from.
.TP
.BR osd\-position " [top|centre|bottom]"
Where the OSD sits.
.TP
.BR layer " [top|overlay]"
Where popups sit relative to fullscreen windows.
.B overlay
(the default) covers them;
.B top
stays below. No layer exists in between \(em fullscreen sits exactly there.
.RS
.PP
.B top
was the default until it became clear that it cannot be told apart from a
fault: the notification is recorded, never shown, and nothing says why. Prefer
.BR dnd " or " quiet\-while\-busy
to ask for quiet, since both say what they are doing.
.RE
.TP
.BR output " [current|primary|" name ]
Which screen surfaces appear on.
.SH CONTENTS
.TP
.BR widgets " [" list |default]
Which widgets the centre shows, and in what order. See
.BR glassosdrc (5).
.TP
.BR module " " name " [on|off]"
Toggle a half of the daemon on its own. Read at startup, so follow with
.BR restart .
.SH SOUND
.TP
.BR sound " [on|off]"
Notification sounds, by freedesktop sound\-theme name. On by default.
.TP
.BR osd\-sound " [on|off]"
Feedback on volume steps and lock keys. Off by default.
.TP
.B sounds
List every sound name your themes provide, and where to put your own.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glassosd (1),
.BR glassosdrc (5)
.SH AUTHORS
The glassosd contributors.
